WEBVTT

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.940
Let's eat!

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.040
Oh, Principal! Hello.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:19.910
Hello.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.080
Hello there.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.460
You eat in the cafeteria too?

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:31.010
Yes, it's very important that I keep in touch with all of you.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.340
Is the food good?

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.930
Yeah! The Chinese Fair is great!

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:42.230
The lunch ladies are experimenting with the
menu to make sure none of you get bored.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.440
Oh, you're all eating together?

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.590
Principal!

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.810
I don't see you in the cafeteria very often.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.070
You usually bring your lunch.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:02.290
Well, the cafeteria's menu is healthy, and it's nice
to mingle with the students from time to time.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:06.290
Don't worry, Principal. You can sit with us.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:07.790
Go ahead.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.970
One, two, three, four!

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:21.020
Two, two, three, four!

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.810
Three, two, three, four!

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.860
Four, two, three, four!

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:31.400
This really clears my head.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.400
It wakes you up, doesn't it?

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.490
Yeah, I pulled another all-nighter, so it's a great change of pace.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.160
Food always tastes best after you've worked out.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.330
It's about time.

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:47.630
All right, let's head back inside.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.340
Hiro!

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:58.760
You're all so mean. What are you eating without me?

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.290
We're not eating anything. We're exercising.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.230
Come on, back to your room.

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:06.560
Really?

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.310
Yes, really.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.020
Get up and get ready for school.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.070
And here I thought Hiro had gotten up early for once.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.770
Is she a sleepwalker?

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.070
Will she be okay?

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:30.790
What!? You haven't had the crab fried rice yet!?

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.550
The crab fried rice from the Chinese Fair special menu!

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.510
It's packed full of crab!

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.400
And it comes with chicken soup! All for only 400 yen!

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.020
What else is on the menu?

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:55.690
Well, there's tenshinhan, pepper steak, prawns in chili sauce, and dandan noodles.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:03:01.240
Some kids in my class are trying to get everything on the menu while they have it.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.120
That sounds like fun.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:08.210
Yeah. The crab fried rice has to be the best part.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:13.130
I can tell how good it is just hearing her talk about it!

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.460
Sae, Hiro, how about you two?

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.130
Yeah, we tried it.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.260
Was it the day before yesterday?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:21.640
There were a lot of other people eating it as well.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.840
Yeah, it seemed pretty popular.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.000
Wow. I wonder if they had to buy more woks.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.110
I don't know about that.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:35.310
And more crab spoons, Miya.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.320
She's hung up on that?

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:42.200
Now I really wanna try some.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:42.990
Same.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.490
I think they only have it till tomorrow.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.200
Really? I'm glad you told us about it today.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.750
That was a close call!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.590
I wanna eat it! I really wanna eat it!

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:57.840
Doggie.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.450
Doggie!?

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:04.120
Sallying forth to the cafeteria!

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.140
Miya, you're going to school.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:10.250
Hey, what kind of crab do they make crab fried rice out of?

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.600
What kind of crab?

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.690
Yeah. They usually use king crab or snow crab,

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:19.990
but those have gotten pretty expensive. So, maybe Hanasaki crab?

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.410
Horsehair crab, spider crab!

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.870
Heikegani, river crab...

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.620
Nah, couldn't be.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.690
Subesubemanjugani!

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.090
Slippery!?

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.440
Good morning, class.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:39.340
Have you gone to the cafeteria's Chinese Fair?

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:42.780
I had some crab fried rice.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.690
It was incredibly tasty.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:50.020
Just adding a little crab made it taste so much like the sea.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:55.230
Let's work on flats of sea life today.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.400
Wow, she just decided on that.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.400
Yunocchi, what are you going to draw?

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:04.190
A scene full of starfish, like the night sky.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:08.010
Miyako's starfish facts!

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:12.940
Starfirsh are called "starfish" or "sea stars" in English.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.900
That sounds so wonderful!

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:21.670
Also, they feed on the carcasses of dead fish.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.930
They shove their stomach out of their body,
wrap it around the carcass, and digest it.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.300
Yunocchi?

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.560
Maybe I won't draw so many.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.100
Anyway, crab fried rice is awesome.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:39.320
It's hard enough making normal fried rice.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.200
It takes eight months to grow the rice.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:47.360
Then to fry it up nice and thick, you need an egg a chicken laid.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.030
And then you need oil and leek.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:56.620
I wonder who thought of mixing in that
crabby critter they fished up from the sea floor.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.060
Back to work.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.490
Miya...

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:07.160
All right, class is over.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:12.260
If you're not done yet, bring your work to me during lunch.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:18.440
Sorry, Miya. I still have work to do, so go have lunch with someone else.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:22.400
What are you saying? I'd never leave you behind!

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.570
We promised we'd go together!

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:30.710
Let's go after school.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:31.830
Okay!

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.290
What are they talking about?

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:38.120
I'm finally done. Cleanup took a while.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.340
Yunocchi, I bought this for you!

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.210
Margarine Roll
puffy and tasty

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.160
A margerine roll!

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.800
Oh, thanks.

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:48.550
Here, Yuno, you can snack on this.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.430
There's Mr. Mashiko.

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:52.040
Tha—

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:55.850
Geez, Mashiko, you're always too on time.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:58.060
All right, let's start class.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.460
Run, Yunocchi, run!

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.740
I'm so hungry!

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:18.240
Sorry, we're sold out.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.460
It's the last day, so we didn't order as many ingredients.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:27.160
It's over. It's all over.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:32.080
Miya, I've... I've done something I can't take back.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.720
What are you talking about?

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.520
Sae! Hiro!

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:44.690
Oh!

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:52.710
Oh, you didn't get to try the crab fried rice?

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:56.920
Yeah. It was my fault.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:02.260
I hope they have another Chinese Fair.

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:03.990
No problem!

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.960
Well then, why don't we do it at my place tonight?

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.590
You don't have to worry about me!

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.710
We didn't mean to drag you into this!

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:18.820
Sae, are they worried about me?

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:20.230
I don't think...

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:28.570
Okay, dig in. I only had imitation crab, though.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:35.990
Delicious!

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.410
Yeah, this is great!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.830
So tasty!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:44.420
Your food and the school's are like two bananas in a pod!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:47.170
I think you mean "two peas in a pod."

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.530
Or "two bananas in a bunch."

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:50.670
Yeah, those!

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:54.200
Seconds, please!

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:58.010
You seem really satisfied.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:02.180
It's just so good!

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.090
Your cooking is magical!

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:09.430
You're a genius!

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:14.110
Hiro's satisfied with her compliments too.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:20.410
That was great. Thanks a lot, Hiro.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.080
Sorry it wasn't real crab.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.330
It's fine.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:28.610
By the way, Nazuna, did you try the cafeteria's crab fried rice?

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:35.550
After you all talked about it, I went and had some today.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:40.100
Nazuna, why didn't you tell me that earlier!?

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.810
I'm sorry!

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:47.740
I wanted to try yours too.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:49.690
It was great.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:51.530
Nazuna...

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:54.650
And it was fun eating with everyone.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:10:00.280
Oh, Nazuna! Tell me whatever you want, and I'll cook it!

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:06.870
Hiro's curry is just as good as her fried rice. Don't you want some?

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:08.380
Yeah!

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:10.900
Okay, you want curry, right?

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:12.620
Yay!

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:13.840
Hey...

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:21.050
Let's see, tomorrow I have gym and math...

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:30.690
There were a lot of wonderful meals today.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:40.740
Crab, crab...

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:48.190
I wonder if she's graded my drawing from today yet.

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:52.460
I tried really hard, but I still barely made the deadline.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:57.050
Five

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:58.050
Four

00:10:58.930 --> 00:10:59.010
Three

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:00.010
Two

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:01.010
One

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:06.930
September 26th~27th

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:06.930
"Eggplants Really Are Great"

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:23.120
Miss Yoshinoya, I brought the bottles and tins from the storage room.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:27.450
Good. I brought enough eggplants for everyone.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:30.330
We've already got the other materials here...

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.840
Okay, we've got all the motifs.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:39.510
This is a pretty eccentric selection for sketching.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.090
Really?

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:44.430
You're the one that thought of it, right?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:45.430
Yes!

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:48.890
Is it supposed to mean something?

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:52.060
Yes, of course!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:12:01.030
What? The point is to provide a variety of different shapes for everyone to draw—

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.990
Good morning.

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:04.870
Good morning.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:09.870
Is the art department holding a schoolwide concours today?

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:10.870
Yeah.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:20.360
Art is, by nature, not a matter of being able to choose which is superior.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:23.680
Individuality is vital.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.260
Principal...

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:32.020
Try not to put too much pressure on the students when judging them.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.350
You're right.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:43.850
I think there is deep meaning in one's will to improve being sparked by

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:51.120
seeing another student's work being commented on,

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:59.880
and thus looking at one's one work and motif from a different angle.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.910
Good morning, class.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:13.480
Today's the schoolwide concours.

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:16.150
Have you gotten everything ready?

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:19.440
At 9:00, I'll be passing out assignments, and then we'll begin.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:24.200
We'll break for lunch, and then stop at 3:00 PM.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:33.210
The review begins at 4:00. We're doing both classes at once, so be sure to be there.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:39.600
Yuno, that's creepy!

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:50.270
There's so many motifs.

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:52.930
And they're all tougher than usual.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:57.810
I have to bring out their individual features.

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:00.900
Bottle, tin, eggplant, string, hat...
[bin, kan, nasu, ito, hatto]

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:06.320
Sensitive sweetheart!?
[binkan na suiitohaato]

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:11.370
The quicker people are already drawing!

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:12.830
I've gotta hurry up.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:22.920
Yunocchi looks confused.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:26.360
That's good enough.

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.340
I've gotta hurry!

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.850
Sorry, Miya. Did I hit you?

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.320
Don't worry. You can do it, Yunocchi.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:51.410
I can't really get the perspective right.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.330
Miss Yoshinoya's watching.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:01.130
Usually she'd give me some advice.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:05.670
I wonder what she thinks of my drawing.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:10.470
Yuno sure has a nice, tight butt.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:16.470
Lunch time!

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.890
I think I'll have the daily special today.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:20.810
Gorgeous!

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:24.980
I want to forget about the concours for a little while and enjoy my meal.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:30.410
Excuse me, what's today's A Special?

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:34.280
A is eggplant and pork stir-fry with miso.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:37.500
Eggplant... Um, how about B?

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:41.120
B is spaghetti with meat sauce and eggplant.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.340
Um... And C?

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:44.920
Szechuan eggplant.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.510
Do you hate me?

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:48.470
What?

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:55.410
There's only a little time left.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.770
I need to focus and draw.

00:15:57.770 --> 00:16:00.480
I don't know what to do.

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.900
All right, time's up.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.770
I'll be collecting the eggplants.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.950
All right, let's compare them.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.440
The upper ones scored better.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:20.120
Review is at 4:00. You're free until then.

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:23.010
What's wrong, Yunocchi?

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:27.090
I'm so scared of the ranking that I can't look.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:31.530
I feel like they're staring at my back.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:32.970
You're right.

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:37.480
I think they're staring at my butt, though.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.900
Oh, I ranked high!

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:45.310
Really? You're great!

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:48.190
Mine is...

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:58.380
Am I just imagining things, or did Yuno get shorter?

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:01.700
She looks even tinier than usual.

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:19.810
What!? I can't take that scene out!

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.690
It's unusual to hear Sae yelling.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.610
I told you, I can't!

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:30.280
Looks like she's on the phone with her editor.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:36.310
I didn't get enough sleep. I was too tense.

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:40.660
If I'd been in proper form... Just a little more!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.410
No way!

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:55.250
This hurts so much.

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:59.680
Why does drawing have to end up like this?

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:04.110
I feel like maybe I should just never show anyone my work.

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:07.720
But then, why do I draw?

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:14.700
I don't think I draw to show people anyway.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:18.600
Why does drawing have to end up like this?

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:21.490
I feel like maybe I should just never—

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:24.500
I almost got caught in a loop!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.500
Anguish!

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:31.790
That's right.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:34.950
When you're sketching, you're judged solely on technique,

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:40.050
so the review can be clear and painful, but you'll get better if you practice.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:43.260
You don't need to worry about it so much.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:47.470
Sorry, I'm just whining.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:50.190
No, it's fine.

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:53.450
Sae!?

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:59.700
Next door, there's another girl who agonizes over her work.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:06.500
Sometimes it seems like Sae is always in the kind of situation you're in now.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:14.920
She's constantly judged by other people while she hones her skills.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.260
It must be very hard on her.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:21.590
Then why does she still keep going?

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:26.520
I don't know. Maybe because she loves it?

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:33.130
I can't take this!

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.170
She's having such a hard time.

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:07.180
Yunocchi!

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:11.260
You're sound asleep.

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:14.190
Did you stay up late?

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:18.940
Art Dept.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:25.650
I can't keep my eyes open.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:28.450
It's okay. You don't need to force yourself to today.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:35.460
Yuno, that's creepy!

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:44.880
The top three jobs that girls want are restaurateur, nurse, and teacher.

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.380
I wanted to be a pâtissière.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:48.400
I wanted to be a mommy!

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:50.340
I wanted to be a daddy!

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:51.460
That's impossible.

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:54.280
Not many people get their dream job, do they?

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.920
How about Miss Yoshinoya?

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.000
That's—

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:02.480
Next time, "November 22nd: Third Years and First Years" and

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.500
"May 21st: The Crying Woman."

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:09.080
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments. Be sure to come see us!
